\begin{aligned}
\color{black}\text{Number of lives after losing 8} &= \color{red}\text{Initial number of lives} - \color{blue}\text{Lives lost} \\
&= 43 - 8 \\
&= \boxed{\textbf{35}}
\end{aligned}

Next, let's find out how many lives she will have after gaining 39 more lives in the next level:

\begin{aligned}
\color{black}\text{Number of lives after gaining 39} &= \color{red}\text{Number of lives after losing 8} + \color{blue}\text{Lives gained} \\
&= 35 + 39 \\
&= \boxed{\textbf{74}}
\end{aligned}

Thus, if Wendy gets 39 more lives in the next level, she will have \boxed{\textbf{74}} lives.

